Chat backend (./chatbackend on the server, not in this repo): load ONE last
message per conversation for the chat list.

The list route used `include: { messages: { orderBy: date desc, take: 1 } }`.
Prisma doesn't limit that in SQL: it reads every message of the page's
conversations and keeps one per conversation in memory, so the list got
heavier as chats grew. Now a LATERAL query reads one row per conversation via
the (conversationId, date) index. Checked before switching: same last message
for all 85 users / 218 conversations.

Applied on the server 2026-10-31 (backup: ~/backups/dm_routes.js.bak-20261031-lastmsg).
Apply after firebase-token-auth.patch:
  cd ~/treepnet/chatbackend && patch -p1 < chat-list-last-message.patch
  cd .. && docker compose build chatbackend && docker compose up -d chatbackend

